# The stack daemon (design/daemons.md, Part 2): dev/devbox's image — nix, a
# stack userland, the grants a dev stack needs, and CAOS_RESIDENT=1 — with this
# directory's script curried onto it. A job for it carries `affinity`, the
# tree under test, so ONE container serves every message for one tree and keeps
# that tree's dev stack running between them.
#
# It is not run by hand. `std/caos-test` and `dev/caos-stack` are the callers:
# each forms the keyed message and tail-calls it.
#
# `--required-caosd=true` pins the daemon to the central host. devbox's grants
# are persistent volumes — the shared nix store (/mounted-nix), the stacks'
# state (/caos-dev) and their engine's images (/caos-images) — which only the
# caosd runner grants, and the dev stack reaches the host's redis and registry
# by name (dev/stack-up). The arg routes every message for the daemon to the
# caosd runner; a plain runnerd (on any machine) never runs it.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/devbox --worker1:@=worker.sh --required-caosd=true
